<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/17th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · Revolt</p><h1 class="enc-title">Fettmilch Uprising</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1612">1612</a>–<a href="/years/1616">1616</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/17th-century">17th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Fettmilch Uprising was a revolt of guildsmen in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/frankfurt">Frankfurt</a> am Main from 1612 to 1616, led by the gingerbread baker Vincenz Fettmilch against the patrician council. In August 1614 the rioters plundered the Judengasse and expelled the city's <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jews">Jews</a>. Imperial intervention restored order: Fettmilch was executed in 1616 and the Jews were brought back under imperial protection.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/fettmilch-uprising.jpg" alt="Fettmilch Uprising" width="320" height="140" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown author · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Fettmilch-Aufstand_Anfuehrer.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
